    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1408">

                <pb facs="1752" n="1552" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/8–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1408<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-07T00:00:00+02:00">August 7,
                        1945—midnight.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4772. The following is translation of note dated August 4 handed to me by
                        Bidault this evening (my 4769, August
                        7<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1408-f1"/>).</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Concerning the communications addressed to it on July 31, August 1 and 2 by
                        the three govts represented at the Potsdam Conference,<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d1408-f2"/> the French Provisional Govt, desirous of avoiding
                        inconveniences (<hi rendition="#italic">inconvénients</hi>) which have
                        occurred in the past, and noting that the communiqué published at the
                        termination of the Potsdam Conference<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1408-f3"/>
                        treats of questions about which it has not been advised, would like to know
                        if the information which has been furnished up to the present time covers
                        the whole of the results of the conference, or if other important decisions
                        have been made, notably with regard to the multiple problems with which the
                        Council of Ministers of the five great powers will have to deal”.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
